From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Anderson <thomasanderson@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:34:06 -0700
Subject: [Wayland] Fix UAF in
 WaylandZwpLinuxDmabuf::NotifyRequestCreateBufferDone

NotifyRequestCreateBufferDone() looked up an iterator into
`pending_params_`, ran the stored callback, and then erased using the
same iterator. The callback can synchronously re-enter CreateBuffer()
(via WaylandBufferHandle::OnWlBufferCreated ->
WaylandFrameManager::MaybeProcessPendingFrame), which emplaces into
`pending_params_`. Since it is a base::flat_map, that insert may
reallocate, leaving the iterator dangling.

Move the callback out of the entry and erase the entry before running
the callback.

Fixed: 574200170
Change-Id: I492e05574d2a836137521102fba16bc07b542528
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8599238
Auto-Submit: Thomas Anderson <thomasanderson@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kramer Ge <fangzhoug@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Kramer Ge <fangzhoug@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1722152}

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_zwp_linux_dmabuf.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_zwp_linux_dmabuf.cc
index 61ac95914e0d569198d4e6391b0c23bc51628ff2..fcd49212f63b1621a534d5d5840b8b1f7042e191 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_zwp_linux_dmabuf.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/wayland/host/wayland_zwp_linux_dmabuf.cc
@@ -183,8 +183,11 @@ void WaylandZwpLinuxDmabuf::NotifyRequestCreateBufferDone(
     return item.first.get();
   });
   CHECK(it != pending_params_.end());
-  std::move(it->second).Run(wl::Object<wl_buffer>(new_buffer));
+  // Erase the entry before running the callback, as the callback may re-enter
+  // CreateBuffer() and modify `pending_params_`, which would invalidate `it`.
+  wl::OnRequestBufferCallback callback = std::move(it->second);
   pending_params_.erase(it);
+  std::move(callback).Run(wl::Object<wl_buffer>(new_buffer));
   connection_->Flush();
 }
 
